from pathlib import Path
from docx import Document

OUT=Path('/data/y01014/diliyaer/BLCA_CAF_project/GDF15_CAF_project/analysis_revisions_20260909/frontiers_manuscripts')
extra=[
'The analytical design used several safeguards against common errors in single-cell studies. First, CAF extraction was performed before downstream state scoring so that lineage contamination could be quantified independently of the biological labels. Second, integration was used to reduce technical cohort effects, but cohort identity and sample identity were retained in all metadata. Third, cell-level patterns were summarized at the patient level before association testing. These decisions were intended to prevent the large number of cells in a single specimen from being treated as independent clinical replicates.',
'The four discovery cohorts differed in sample composition, tissue context, and data-generation characteristics. Rather than forcing complete equivalence, the analysis asked whether the same state axes could be recognized across cohorts after harmonized annotation. A state was considered more credible when it retained coherent marker-module scores, appeared in more than one cohort, and remained interpretable after contamination audit. This criterion is stricter than assigning a biological name to every computational cluster and is appropriate for a cross-cohort CAF atlas.',
'The program-construction strategy also separated gene selection from clinical evaluation. The 19 genes were selected from repeated perturbation-derived outputs before the TCGA models were interpreted. The clinical analysis therefore evaluated a fixed program rather than repeatedly selecting genes in the survival cohort. Nevertheless, because the program was derived computationally and the external cohorts were retrospective, the resulting hazard ratios should be regarded as estimates of association and not as evidence of a validated clinical assay.',
'The patient-level CAF–myeloid analysis was deliberately interpreted at the level of coordinated states. Myeloid fraction, myeloid score, exhaustion score, and cytotoxicity score are related but non-equivalent quantities. A positive association with one measure does not imply an increase in every myeloid population or a uniform change in immune function. The cohort-dependent effect sizes reinforce this point and suggest that future studies should measure cell composition, activation state, spatial position, and treatment exposure jointly.',
'The spatial analysis provides an important boundary on the interpretation of the bulk and single-cell results. ECM–myeloid co-variation was present in subsets of spatial samples, but CCDC80 itself was not uniformly stable across patients. This pattern is compatible with a broader ECM-associated state in which CCDC80 is a representative gene rather than a universal spatial marker. It also argues against using CCDC80 immunoreactivity alone as a surrogate for the entire program without validating the surrounding gene and protein context.',
'The external validation layers were not treated as interchangeable replications. Bulk expression cohorts test whether the program can be measured in mixed tissue, while spatial data test local co-occurrence and IMvigor210 provides a treatment-context analysis. Each layer has different sources of bias and different biological resolution. Agreement across layers increases confidence in the existence of a reproducible association, but it does not eliminate confounding from tissue composition, platform, treatment history, or clinical selection.',
'The results have practical implications for experimental design. A perturbation study should compare CCDC80-associated program activity with CAF abundance and should include matrix production, matrix organization, and myeloid-cell behavior as separate readouts. A communication experiment should test prioritized ligand–receptor pairs with receptor blockade or ligand depletion and should measure both CAF and myeloid responses. These experiments would distinguish a marker of a matrix-active state from a molecule that is necessary for the observed phenotype.',
'Finally, the current analysis supports a staged translational path. The first stage is analytical replication in additional bladder-cancer single-cell and spatial cohorts. The second is orthogonal measurement by multiplex imaging or targeted spatial assays. The third is functional perturbation in CAF–myeloid systems. Only after these stages should a prospective study evaluate whether the program adds prognostic or predictive value beyond stage, CAF abundance, molecular subtype, and established immune biomarkers.'
]
for path in sorted(OUT.glob('CCDC80_CAF_ECM_myeloid_Frontiers_*.docx')):
    doc=Document(path)
    target=next(p for p in doc.paragraphs if p.text.strip()=='Discussion')
    for text in reversed(extra):
        p=target.insert_paragraph_before(text)
        p.style='Normal'
    doc.save(path)
    print(path)
